  "verdict": "THRESHOLD_IS_THE_BINDING_CONSTRAINT",
  "why": "14 of 21 O-unresolved isolates DO hit an O allele below the deployed 90.0/80.0 cut, so the information is already in the DB and the earlier 'DB coverage / data engineering' claim was WRONG. NOTE: this does NOT license lowering the threshold -- that trades abstentions for wrong calls, and the wrong-call cost is NOT measured here.",
  "honest_limits": [
    "A permissive hit means the INFORMATION is present, NOT that admitting it is safe. Lowering the cut trades abstentions for wrong calls and that cost is NOT measured here; abstention is the safer failure.",
    "Only the O-unresolved abstentions are probed -- this says nothing about the H axes or about isolates that already resolve.",
    "One antigen-DB build (62 O alleles) and one cohort. A different DB changes the answer."
  ],
  "sub_threshold_correctness": {
    "n": 14,
    "names_correct_O_group": 14,
    "names_wrong_O_group": 0,
    "meaning": "every sub-threshold hit names the RIGHT O group, so the rejected alignments are correct matches, not noise"
  },
  "sub_threshold_shape": {
    "O_group_counts": {
      "7": 11,
      "40": 1,
      "18": 1,
      "3,10": 1
    },
    "identity_median": 99.8,
    "coverage_median": 58.35,
    "coverage_max": 78.9,
    "mechanism": "near-perfect IDENTITY (median 99.8) at PARTIAL COVERAGE (median 58.4, max 78.9 -- all below the deployed 80 cut), concentrated on the O7 wzx/wzy allele (11 of 14)"
  },
  "what_is_still_NOT_established": [
    "WHETHER to change anything. Two causal claims about this cell were asserted and then measured wrong in a row (first phase-2 flagellin, then DB coverage); the wrong-call cost of relaxing the coverage cut is the THIRD such claim and it is NOT measured here.",
    "Whether the right fix is the coverage threshold, the O7 reference allele itself, or partial-alignment handling. The concentration on one O group argues for an allele-level cause, but that is a hypothesis.",
    "Infantis appears in BOTH the sub-threshold (3) and the no-hit (4) buckets, so O7 detection is inconsistent even within one serovar -- unexplained."
  ]
